This makes the assumption that the recover will always work... Or the
game has one. I make it a habit to make backups of saves for all my
roguelikes... I HAVE save scummed a few times in various games, but
those were nonserious games. But, far outweighing the times I've
scummed are the times I've used it the backup for power
outages/computer crashes. Mm. Anyone that's had FPnL (Florida Plunder
and Loot ... Power and Light) as a power provider knows that random
power outages can happen pretty often. It isn't always scumming.

Though, in the case of the parakeet example... What's acceptable there?
If you load a save because of something like that, is it scumming? It
IS a bit of an unfair advantage to know what's coming... But, I had a
nephew mess with my computer while I was playing IVAN, and ended up
getting killed - without a backup. I was pretty far and, needless to
say, I wasn't happy. I wish I had had a backup in that case.



